# differences for dead or not dead vampire, and fast healing improves after level 5
Coffin Sanctuary	DESC:You have chosen a coffin or similar small enclosed space as your primary resting place. If you reach -1 to -9 HP while outside the coffin, you are forced to assume gaseous form immediately and flee to your coffin to teal. If you cannot enter gaseous form for any reason, you die immediately. If your gaseous form ability expires before you reach your coffin, or more than 2 hours pass, you return to your normal form and begin to die. If you reach your coffin, you are helpless for 1 hour, after which you heal 1HP and are no longer helpless. A non-helpless vampire in his coffin has fast healing 1.|!PRETEMPLATE:1,Undead|PREVAREQ:VampireCoffinSanctuaryLVL,1	DESC:You have chosen a coffin or similar small enclosed space as your primary resting place. If you reach -1 to -9 HP while outside the coffin, you are forced to assume gaseous form immediately and flee to your coffin to teal. If you cannot enter gaseous form for any reason, you die immediately. If your gaseous form ability expires before you reach your coffin, or more than 2 hours pass, you return to your normal form and begin to die. If you reach your coffin, you are helpless for 1 hour, after which you heal 1HP and are no longer helpless. A non-helpless vampire in his coffin has fast healing 5.|!PRETEMPLATE:1,Undead|PREVAREQ:VampireCoffinSanctuaryLVL,2	DESC:You have chosen a coffin or similar small enclosed space as your primary resting place. If you reach 0 or fewer HP while outside the coffin, you are forced to assume gaseous form immediately and flee to your coffin to teal. If you cannot enter gaseous form for any reason, you die immediately. If your gaseous form ability expires before you reach your coffin, or more than 2 hours pass, you are destroyed. If you reach your coffin, you are helpless for 1 hour, after which you heal 1HP and are no longer helpless. A non-helpless vampire in his coffin has fast healing 1.|PRETEMPLATE:1,Undead|PREVAREQ:VampireCoffinSanctuaryLVL,1	DESC:You have chosen a coffin or similar small enclosed space as your primary resting place. If you reach 0 or fewer HP while outside the coffin, you are forced to assume gaseous form immediately and flee to your coffin to teal. If you cannot enter gaseous form for any reason, you die immediately. If your gaseous form ability expires before you reach your coffin, or more than 2 hours pass, you are destroyed. If you reach your coffin, you are helpless for 1 hour, after which you heal 1HP and are no longer helpless. A non-helpless vampire in his coffin has fast healing 5.|PRETEMPLATE:1,Undead|PREVAREQ:VampireCoffinSanctuaryLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireCoffinSanctuaryLVL 1-2

Dominate	DESC:A vampire can crush anothers will just by looking into their eyes. This is a gaze attack, except that you must use a standard action. Anyone you target must make a will save or instantly fall under your influence (as though 'dominate' spell, 12th lvl caster). This ability has a range of 5' and is usable once per day.|PREVAREQ:VampireDominateLVL,1	DESC:A vampire can crush anothers will just by looking into their eyes. This is a gaze attack, except that you must use a standard action. Anyone you target must make a will save or instantly fall under your influence (as though 'dominate' spell, 12th lvl caster). This ability has a range of 10' and is usable three times per day.|PREVAREQ:VampireDominateLVL,2	DESC:A vampire can crush anothers will just by looking into their eyes. This is a gaze attack, except that you must use a standard action. Anyone you target must make a will save or instantly fall under your influence (as though 'dominate' spell, 12th lvl caster). This ability has a range of 30' and is usable three times per day.|PREVAREQ:VampireDominateLVL,3	DESC:A vampire can crush anothers will just by looking into their eyes. This is a gaze attack, except that you must use a standard action. Anyone you target must make a will save or instantly fall under your influence (as though 'dominate' spell, 12th lvl caster). This ability has a range of 30' and is usable at will.|PREVAREQ:VampireDominateLVL,4	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireDominateLVL 1-4

Vampire Gaseous Form	DESC:You can assume gaseous form as the spell (5th lvl caster), once per day as a standard action. You can remain gaseous for 10 minutes. Whilst gaseous your fly speed is 20'|PREVAREQ:VampireGaseousFormLVL,1	DESC:You can assume gaseous form as the spell (5th lvl caster), three times per day as a standard action. You can remain gaseous for 10 minutes. Whilst gaseous your fly speed is 20'|PREVAREQ:VampireGaseousFormLVL,2	DESC:You can assume gaseous form as the spell (5th lvl caster), at will, as a standard action. You can remain gaseous indefinately. Whilst gaseous your fly speed is 20'|PREVAREQ:VampireGaseousFormLVL,3	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireGaseousFormLVL 1-3

# not leveled
Aversions	DESC:You have the 'classic' aversions of vampire kind. You cannot tolerate the strong odor of garlic, and cannot enter an area laced with it. Similarly you recoil from a mirror or a strongly presented holy symbol. These items do not harm you, they merely keep you at bat. You must stay at least 5' away from a creature holding a mirror or holy symbol and cannot touch or make melee attacks against that creature for the rest of the encounter. Holding you at bay like this requires your opponent to take a standard action. You are also unable to cross running water, though you can be carried over it while resting in your coffin, or aboard a ship. You are utterly unable to enter a home or other building unless invited in by someone with the authority to do so. You may freely enter public places.	CATEGORY:Special Ability
# add PRE for natural swim speed to override

Alternate Form	DESC:You can assume the shape of a bat or wolf as a standard action. Similar to the polymorph spell (12th lvl caster), except that you do not gain HP from changing form. Whilst in an alternate form you lose your slam attack and dominate ability, but gain the natural weapons and extraordinary attacks of your new form. You can remain in your new form until you assume another form, or the next sunrise.|PREVAREQ:VampireAlternateFormLVL,1	DESC:You can assume the shape of a bat or wolf, or dire versions of either, as a standard action. Similar to the polymorph spell (12th lvl caster), except that you do not gain HP from changing form. Whilst in an alternate form you lose your slam attack and dominate ability, but gain the natural weapons and extraordinary attacks of your new form. You can remain in your new form until you assume another form, or the next sunrise.|PREVAREQ:VampireAlternateFormLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireAlternateFormLVL 1-2

Sunlight Vulnerability	DESC:A vampire exposed to direct sunlight is disoriented. While in this condition, you can only take a single move action or attack action in a round, and 3 full rounds of such exposure will destroy you utterly.|PREVAREQ:VampireSunlightVulnerabilityLVL,1	DESC:A vampire exposed to direct sunlight is disoriented. While in this condition, you can only take a single move action or attack action in a round, and the following round of such exposure will destroy you utterly.|PREVAREQ:VampireSunlightVulnerabilityLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireSunlightVulnerabilityLVL 1-2

Water Vulnerability	DESC:Immersing you in running water robs you of 1/5 your HP each round until you are destroyed at the end of the 5th round of immersion.|PREVAREQ:VampireWaterVulnerabilityLVL,1	DESC:Immersing you in running water robs you of 1/3 your HP each round until you are destroyed at the end of the 3rd round of immersion.|PREVAREQ:VampireWaterVulnerabilityLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#TODO - note vampires with a natural swim speed are not harmed by water.
#VampireWaterVulnerabilityLVL 1-2

Children of the Night	DESC:You can command the lesser creatures of the world. You can call forth a rat swarm, bat swarm or 1d3 wolves as a standard action once per day. The creatures arrive in 2d6 rounds and serve you for up to 1 hour.|PREVAREQ:VampireChildrenOfTheNight,1	DESC:You can command the lesser creatures of the world. You can call forth 1d6+1 rat swarm, 1d4+1 bat swarm or a pack of 3d6 wolves as a standard action once per day. The creatures arrive in 2d6 rounds and serve you for up to 1 hour.|PREVAREQ:VampireChildrenOfTheNight,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireChildrenOfTheNight 1-2

# TODO - worth noting that from when a vampire has damage reduction, its own natural attacks (slam) count as magical for damage resistance reduction

Vampire Energy Drain	DESC:Your slam attack (or any other natural weapon you possess) deals one negative level to any living creature hit. You gain 5 temporary HP for such an attack. You can use this once per round.|PREVAREQ:VampireEnergyDrainLVL,1	DESC:Your slam attack (or any other natural weapon you possess) deals two negative levels to any living creature hit. You gain 5 temporary HP for such an attack. You can use this once per round.|PREVAREQ:VampireEnergyDrainLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	VISIBLE:YES
#VampireEnergyDrainLVL 1-2

Create Spawn	DESC:A humanoid or monstrous humanoid slain by your energy drain attack rises as a vampire spawn after 1d4 days after burial. If you've drained its Con score to 0 or lower, it returns as a spawn if it had 4 or fewer HD, and as a vampire if it had 5 or more HD. In either case, its under your command.You may have no more HD of enslaved spawn than your own HitDice.|PREVAREQ:VampireCreateSpawnLVL,1	DESC:A humanoid or monstrous humanoid slain by your energy drain attack rises as a vampire spawn after 1d4 days after burial. If you've drained its Con score to 0 or lower, it returns as a spawn if it had 4 or fewer HD, and as a vampire if it had 5 or more HD. In either case, its under your command.You may have no more HD of enslaved spawn than twice your own HitDice.|PREVAREQ:VampireCreateSpawnLVL,2	CATEGORY:Special Ability
#VampireCreateSpawnLVL 1-2

Spell-Like Abilities Grigg			KEY:Grig ~ Spell-Like Abilities				CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack																		VISIBLE:YES																					DESC:%1/day - disguise self, entangle (DC 13), invisibility (self only), pyrotechnics (DC 14), ventriloquism (DC 13). Caster level 9th. The save DCs are Charisma-based.|GriggSpellsPerDay


###Block - Anthropomorphic Races





Racial Traits ~ Anthropomorphic Wolf	CATEGORY:Internal	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=Anthropomorphic Wolf Race Trait

Trip		KEY:Anthropomorphic Wolf ~ Trip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Anthropomorphic Wolf Race Trait.SpecialAttack	SOURCEPAGE:p.217	DESC:An anthropomorphic wolf that hits with a bite attack can attempt to trip the opponent as a free action without making a touch attack or provoking an attack of opportunity. If the attempt fails, the opponent cannot react to trip the wolf.
Tracking	KEY:Anthropomorphic Wolf ~ Tracking	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Anthropomorphic Wolf Race Trait.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.217	DESC:Anthropomorphic wolves have a +4 racial bonus on Survival checks when tracking by scent		ASPECT:SkillBonus|+4 racial bonus on Survival checks when tracking by scent	BONUS:SITUATION|Survival=Tracking by Scent|4|TYPE=Racial



###Block - New Monsters

# Thri-kreen
#Poison (Ex): A thri-kreen delivers its poison (Fortitude save DC 11) with a successful bite attack. The initial and secondary damage is the same (paralysis for 2d6 minutes). A thri-kreen produces enough poison for one bite per day.
#Psionics (Sp): *When using the Psionics Handbook, apply the following psionic abilities to a thri-kreen. At will- chameleon, know direction; 1/day-displacement, lesser metaphysical weapon. Manifester level 10th; save DC 8 + power level.
#Attack/Defense Modes: ego whip, mind thrust/thought shield, empty mind. A thri-kreen manifests powers, and gains additional attack and defense modes, as if it were a psychic warrior or a psion with Psychometabolism as its primary discipline. (A psionic thri-kreen character's favored class is psychic warrior, though a few choose monk or psion with the primary discipline of Psychometabolism.) The level adjustment of a thri-kreen with psionics becomes +3.
#Immunity to Sleep (Ex): Since thri-kreen do not sleep, they are immune to magic sleep effects. A thri-kreen spellcaster still requires 8 hours of rest before preparing spells.
#Leap (Ex): A thri-kreen is a natural jumper. It gains a +30 competence bonus on all Jump checks, and its maximum jumping distance is not limited by height.
#Skills: *The exoskeleton of a thri-kreen blends in well with desert terrain, granting it a +4 racial bonus on Hide checks in sandy or arid settings.
#Weapon Familiarity: Thri-kreens treat gythka and chatkcha (see Chapter 5: Equipment) as martial weapons rather than as exotic weapons. Gythka and chatkcha are far more common among thri-kreen than among other races.

Implant		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Implant		TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:A slaad brooder gains the ability to implant pellets with any of his natural attacks. If he previously had a similar ability (red slaad's implant ability or blue slaad's disease ability), he can now use that ability with any of his natural attacks. The affected creature must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + slaad brooder's character level + slaad brooder's Con modifier) to avoid implantation. The egg gestates for one week before hatching into a slaad that eats his way out, killing the host. Twenty-four hours before the egg fully matures, the host falls extremely ill (—10 to all ability scores). A remove disease spell rids a host of the pellet, as does a successful Heal check (DC 20). If the check fails, the healer can try again, but each attempt (successful or not) deals 1d4 points of damage to the patient.  If the brooder is a blue slaad, the pellet hatches into a red slaad. If the brooder is a red slaad, the pellet hatches into a blue slaad. If the host is an arcane spellcaster, the egg pellet instead hatches into a green slaad. [Fortitude DC: (SlaadBrooderImplantDC)]			DEFINE:SlaadBrooderImplantDC|0	BONUS:VAR|SlaadBrooderImplantDC|SlaadBrooderLVL+10+CON+SlaadBrooderImplantDCBonus		DEFINE:SlaadBrooderImplantDC|0	BONUS:VAR|SlaadBrooderImplantDC|2|PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Feat,Ability Focus (Slaad Brooder ~ Implant)

Improved Grab	KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Improved Grab		TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:If a slaad brooder hits with one or more claw or rake attacks, it deals normal damage and attempts to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. The ability works only against opponents of the same size or smaller. The slaad brooder has the option to conduct the grapple normally, or simply use its natural weapons to hold the opponent. Each successful grapple check it makes during successive rounds automatically deals bite damage.	SERVESAS:ABILITY=Special Ability|Improved Grab

Imbue Pellet	KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Imbue Pellet	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Slaad Brooder Class Feature		CATEGORY:Special Ability		DESC:At 2nd level, a slaad brooder imbues a single egg pellet with an additional feature randomly determined from the options described below [roll d4 and apply the appropriate feature]. This feature affects the host as indicated. Where a save is permitted, the DC is (ImbuePelletDC). Roll separately for each implant attack.  1. Burn: The pellet deals 1d6 points of heat damage to the host on the round of implantation. A successful Fortitude save halves the damage. The pellet deals an additional 1d6 points of heat damage on the next round unless the host makes a successful Fortitude save.      2. Caustic: As the burn feature, except that the damage is acid damage.      3. Chill: As the burn feature, except that the damage is cold damage.      4. Shock: As the burn feature, except that the damage is electricity damage.		DEFINE:ImbuePelletDC|0	BONUS:VAR|ImbuePelletDC|10+SlaadBrooderLVL+CON

Deep Implant	KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Deep Implant	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:At 3rd level, a slaad brooder can implant his pellet more deeply within the host's body, adding +2 to the DC of the Fortitude save to resist implantation. In addition, repeated Heal checks after the first to remove the pellet deal 1d6 points of damage to the patient instead of the usual 1d4 points, as the healer must cut more deeply into the host's body.		BONUS:VAR|SlaadBrooderImplantDCBonus|2

Rapid Hatching		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Rapid Hatching	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:On reaching 4th level, a slaad brooder gains the ability to transfer some of his own vitality into the egg pellet, allowing it to mature more quickly. The egg hatches in 24 hours instead of 1 week. Six hours before it hatches, the host comes down with the severe illness, losing 10 points from each ability score.

Chaos Focus			KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Chaos Focus		TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Slaad Brooder Class Feature		CATEGORY:Special Ability		DESC:At 5th level, a slaad brooder's imbue pellet ability becomes more potent: The DC to halve or negate the damage from the additional feature of the pellet (burn, caustic, chill, or shock) increases by +2.		BONUS:VAR|ImbuePelletDC|2

Multiple Implant	KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Multiple Implant	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:At 6th level, a slaad brooder can implant more than one pellet within the host's body. Each of his natural attacks that hits can implant an egg pellet.

Color Choice		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Color Choice		TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:At 7th level, a slaad brooder can choose the color of his spawn. He can produce a green slaad even if the host creature is not an arcane spellcaster. He can determine the color of each pellet's spawn if he has implanted more than one in the same host.

Heighten Chaos		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Heighten Chaos		TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Slaad Brooder Class Feature		CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:At 8th level, the DC to halve or negate the damage from the additional feature of an egg pellet increases by +2. This bonus stacks with the bonus provided by the chaos focus ability.		BONUS:VAR|ImbuePelletDC|2

Corporeal Instability		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Corporeal Instability			TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Slaad Brooder Class Feature		CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC: On reaching 9th level, a slaad brooder can effect a terrible transformation on the host creature. Unless she makes a successful Fortitude save [DC (10+SlaadBrooderLVL+CON)], the host's shape melts into a formless mass. She cannot hold or use any item, nor can she wear clothing or armor. Her speed drops to 10 feet or one-quarter normal, whichever is lower. She can no longer cast spells or use magic items, and she cannot distinguish between friend and foe, attacking blindly [—4 penalty on attack rolls, 50%% miss chance].  For each round the host spends in an amorphous state, she takes 1 point of permanent Wisdom drain from mental shock. If the creature's Wisdom score falls to 0, she becomes catatonic and unresponsive. A creature can regain her own shape for 1 minute with a successful Charisma check (DC 15). On a failure, the creature can still repeat the check each round until successful.     A shapechange or stoneskin spell fixes the affected creature's form for the duration of the spell, although it does not cure the affliction. The corporeal instability can be removed with a restoration, greater restoration, or heal spell; a separate restoration spell is required to restore Wisdom drain.

Death Spawn		KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Death Spawn		TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	DESC:At 9th level, a slaad brooder's extraordinary vitality gives his egg pellets the ability to hatch even from a host that has died (the death of a host becomes an increasingly likely event as a brooder becomes more powerful). Neither remove disease spells nor Heal checks can destroy the pellets growing in a dead host, but destruction of the body by fire, acid, disintegrate spells, and the like will do so.

Dominate Spawn	KEY:Slaad Brooder ~ Dominate Spawn		TYPE:SpecialQuality.SpellLike.Slaad Brooder Class Feature	CATEGORY:Special Ability		DESC: On reaching 10th level, the slaad brooder becomes the undisputed master of spawn. If he is present at the hatching of a red, blue, or green slaad, he can take control of the newborn as with a dominate monster spell. The effect lasts one day per slaad brooder's character level. The hatchling can resist the effect with a successful Will save [DC (10 +SlaadBrooderLVL+CON)].  A slaad brooder that has reached this level of power is a threat to the dominance of death slaadi, who are his implacable enemies.

Blindsight		CATEGORY:Special Ability	KEY:Anthropomorphic Baleen Whale ~ Blindsight	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Blindsight	DESC: 60' on land, 120' in water.  Negated by silence.  
Hold Breath			CATEGORY:Special Ability	KEY:Anthropomorphic Baleen Whale ~ Hold Breath	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Hold Breath	DESC:A Whale can hold its breath for 8x it's constitution score rounds before it risks drowning.  

